{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2170-03-23 20:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be your doctor during this stay. Can you tell me what brought you in today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2170-03-23 20:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi. I’ve had a sore throat, cough, and chest pain when I cough. Also, I’ve been vomiting for about three days now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2170-03-23 20:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Any fever or chills?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2170-03-23 20:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No fever, but I’ve had chills. And I feel dizzy sometimes, especially when I stand up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2170-03-23 20:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. The ER gave you fluids and an antibiotic, ceftriaxone. We’re going to hold off on more antibiotics for now and see what’s going on."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2170-03-23 20:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "But I had a similar infection a few weeks ago. They found H. influenza and gave me levofloxacin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2170-03-23 20:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, I see that. But you only took three days of it because you started vomiting and having stomach pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2170-03-23 20:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Right. The nausea and vomiting started right after I took the levofloxacin. I think it was the antibiotic causing it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2170-03-23 20:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s possible. Levofloxacin can cause stomach upset. We’ve stopped it, and we’ll focus on managing your symptoms."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2170-03-23 20:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I’m not getting any antibiotics now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2170-03-23 20:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not right now. You’re not running a fever, and your exam doesn’t show signs of active infection. We’ll monitor you closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2170-03-23 20:41:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. But my throat still hurts, and coughing is painful."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2170-03-23 20:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll manage your pain with acetaminophen and add naproxen if needed. We also have a lidocaine-based spray for your throat."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2170-03-23 20:43:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I have something stronger? Oxycodone usually helps with the chest pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2170-03-23 20:44:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand, but because of past issues with your pain medication agreement, we’re avoiding opioids for now. We’ll use non-opioid options that are safer."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2170-03-23 20:45:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I guess that’s fair. I just want to feel better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2170-03-23 20:46:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll get there. We’ve started IV fluids because your labs show mild dehydration—low sodium and bicarbonate."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2170-03-23 20:47:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, okay. I haven’t been able to keep much down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2170-03-23 20:48:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. The fluids will help with that and your dizziness. We’ll also check your blood pressure more closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2170-03-24 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your blood work came back. No signs of infection—white count is normal, and blood cultures show no growth."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2170-03-24 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not an infection?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2170-03-24 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not right now. The vomiting and nausea seem more likely due to the levofloxacin side effect. Your cough and throat pain are probably from your usual airway issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2170-03-24 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about the chest X-ray? Did it show anything?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2170-03-24 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It showed a slight shadow on the left, but it’s likely due to how you were positioned. No pneumonia or fluid. Your lungs look stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2170-03-24 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good to hear. My breathing feels a bit better today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2170-03-24 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great. We’ll keep supporting your airway with your usual nebulizers and saline treatments."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2170-03-24 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The interventional pulmonology team reviewed your case. They agree you don’t need more antibiotics right now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2170-03-24 14:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "They think it’s safe to go without them?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2170-03-24 14:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. You’re afebrile, stable, and your symptoms are improving. They’ll see you for follow-up in clinic."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2170-03-24 14:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thanks. What about my dizziness?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2170-03-24 14:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We checked your blood pressure when lying and standing—no big drop. But we think it’s partly from dehydration and low blood pressure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2170-03-24 14:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My blood pressure has been low before. I’m on lisinopril for my diabetes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2170-03-24 14:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Right. We’ve held your lisinopril for now because your systolic pressure is in the 100s. We don’t want it dropping too low."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2170-03-24 14:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I shouldn’t take it at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2170-03-24 14:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not until we’re sure your blood pressure is stable. Talk to your PCP before restarting it. They might lower the dose."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2170-03-25 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "How are you feeling today? Any vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2170-03-25 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I haven’t vomited since yesterday morning. I even had some soup."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2170-03-25 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s excellent progress. Your dizziness is better too?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2170-03-25 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, especially after the IV fluids. But I still get a bit lightheaded when I walk."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2170-03-25 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "A physical therapist saw you and thinks vestibular therapy could help. We’re sending a referral for outpatient rehab."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2170-03-25 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That sounds good. I’d like to feel steadier on my feet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2170-03-26 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing really well. We’re planning to discharge you tomorrow morning if things keep improving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2170-03-26 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What meds should I take when I go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2170-03-26 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All your usual meds—metformin, gabapentin, omeprazole, inhalers. But continue holding lisinopril for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2170-03-26 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the naproxen for pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2170-03-26 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, take it as needed for throat or chest pain. But not more than twice a day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2170-03-26 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Any restrictions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2170-03-26 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just take it easy for a few days. Stay hydrated, and follow up with your PCP and pulmonologist."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2170-03-27 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—you’re cleared to go home. Your vitals are stable, and you’re tolerating food well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2170-03-27 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I feel much better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2170-03-27 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll send you home with instructions, your meds, and the vestibular therapy referral."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2170-03-27 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And I’ll see my doctors soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2170-03-27 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your PCP and pulmonologist already have appointments scheduled. Call if you develop fever, vomiting, or trouble breathing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2170-03-27 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks for taking care of me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2170-03-27 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2170-03-23 20:24:00",
    "admission_end": "2170-03-27 14:42:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A young woman with a complex history of tracheobronchomalacia, bronchopulmonary dysplasia, tracheostomy dependence, and type 2 diabetes was admitted for sore throat, cough, chest pain, and three days of vomiting. She had recently taken levofloxacin for a prior tracheitis episode, which was discontinued due to nausea and vomiting likely caused by the antibiotic. Evaluation revealed no active infection—blood cultures were negative, and imaging showed no pneumonia. Her symptoms improved with supportive care, including IV fluids and non-opioid pain management. Hypotension and dizziness were attributed to hypovolemia, leading to temporary discontinuation of lisinopril. She was discharged home in stable condition with instructions to hold lisinopril until PCP follow-up, continue home medications, and attend vestibular physical therapy for dizziness.",
    "problems": [
      "Nausea with vomiting, unspecified",
      "Acute tracheitis without obstruction",
      "Unspecified chronic bronchitis",
      "Unspecified asthma, uncomplicated",
      "Gastro-esophageal reflux disease without esophagitis",
      "Stenosis of larynx",
      "Type 2 diabetes mellitus without complications",
      "Major depressive disorder, single episode, unspecified",
      "Essential (primary) hypertension",
      "Other diseases of bronchus, not elsewhere classified",
      "Dyskinesia of esophagus",
      "Hypovolemia",
      "Proteinuria, unspecified",
      "Hypotension, unspecified",
      "Tracheostomy status",
      "Adverse effect of other systemic antibiotics, initial encounter",
      "Personal history of (corrected) congenital malformations of respiratory system"
    ]
  }
}
